{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.sign_law_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.sign_law_general","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L230-L239","doc":"**(CONDITIONAL on the conjecture.)**  If the Milnor-parity conjecture holds for a\ntrace family `τ`, then at every Brunnian order `A ≥ 2` (with `E₀ > 0`, `h ≠ 0`) the\nbinding cluster `E₀·(1 − τ A h)` has sign `(−1)^(A−1)`.  Fully verified by Lean\nmodulo the single open class instance `MilnorParitySignConjecture τ` (§3b-cond\nconditional result — the conjecture is the only unproved input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.MilnorParitySignConjecture.crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.MilnorParitySignConjecture.crossing","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L228-L228","doc":"The parity crossing pattern at every Brunnian order `A ≥ 2` and nonzero `h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.MilnorParitySignConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.MilnorParitySignConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L226-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.MilnorParitySignConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.MilnorParitySignConjecture","kind":"class","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L213-L228","doc":"**(CONJECTURE, primary — OPEN.)**  The general Milnor-parity sign law, stated\nfor a candidate `A`-indexed Brunnian level-trace family `τ : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ`\n(`τ A h` = level trace of the length-`A` iterated commutator at `h = q − q⁻¹`):\nthe parity crossing pattern holds at *every* Brunnian order `A ≥ 2` and every\nnonzero `h`.  For the *actual* Brunnian Markov-trace family this asserts the\nuniversal alternation `sign(1 − τ_A) = (−1)^(A−1)`.\n\nThis carrier has **NO instance** — the honest open state — because the pattern is\nconfirmed at only two orders (A=3 PROVED, A=4 MEASURED; #4360/#4378) and no general\ntopological derivation of the order law or the crossing sign exists in the corpus.\nFabricating an instance would launder the two-point pattern into a universal claim\n(forbidden by the anti-laundering discipline).  The field is content-bearing (a\nparameter-quantified inequality in the shape of the claim), not an empty marker. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.parity_sign_flip_a3_a4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.parity_sign_flip_a3_a4","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L204-L209","doc":"**Both confirmed data points together — the A=3→A=4 Milnor-parity sign flip.**\n`paritySign 3 = +1` (deficit `+`, PROVED) and `paritySign 4 = −1` (deficit `−`,\nMEASURED): the sign alternates with `A` per `(−1)^(A−1)` across the two orders for\nwhich the crossing pattern is confirmed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.sign_law_A4_measured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.sign_law_A4_measured","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L195-L202","doc":"**A=4 instance.**  The genuine Brunnian cluster is negative and\n`paritySign 4 = −1` — sign `−`, with the crossing hypothesis discharged by\nMEASUREMENT (τ_L₄ > 1), not proof.  The `(−1)^(A−1)` convention is confirmed at the\nsecond data point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.crossing_A4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.crossing_A4","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L189-L193","doc":"A=4 discharges the crossing hypothesis by the **MEASURED** `τ_L₄ > 1` (#4378,\ncited).  This is NOT a proved closed form — the input is the measurement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.sign_law_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.sign_law_A3","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L182-L187","doc":"**A=3 instance.**  The Borromean cluster is positive and `paritySign 3 = +1` —\nsign `+`, fully PROVED (order + sign, from #4360's closed form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.crossing_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.crossing_A3","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L177-L180","doc":"A=3 discharges the crossing hypothesis by the **PROVED** `τ_Borr < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.sign_law_of_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.sign_law_of_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L149-L173","doc":"**(CONDITIONAL sign law — the star result.)**  For `A ≥ 1`, positive energy\nscale `E₀`, and a level trace `τ` satisfying the parity crossing pattern, the sign\nof the `A`-body Brunnian binding cluster `c_A = E₀·(1 − τ)` equals `(−1)^(A−1)`:\npositive exactly when `paritySign A = 1` (odd A), negative exactly when\n`paritySign A = −1` (even A).  Nothing here is assumed proved beyond the explicit\n`CrossingPattern` hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.CrossingPattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.CrossingPattern","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L142-L147","doc":"**Parity crossing pattern** for an `A`-component Brunnian level trace `τ`: the\ndeficit `1 − τ` is positive for odd `A` (`τ < 1`) and negative for even `A`\n(`τ > 1`).  This is the empirically-observed / hypothesized pattern — it is used\nbelow only as an explicit HYPOTHESIS (§3b-cond), never asserted as proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.paritySign_of_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.paritySign_of_even","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L135-L138","doc":"Convention lemma: for even `A ≥ 1`, `(−1)^(A−1) = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.paritySign_of_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.paritySign_of_odd","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L130-L133","doc":"Convention lemma: for odd `A`, `(−1)^(A−1) = +1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.paritySign_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.paritySign_four","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.paritySign_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.paritySign_three","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L127-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.paritySign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.paritySign","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L123-L125","doc":"Parity sign value `(−1)^(A−1)` in `ℤ` (`ℕ`-subtraction; well-defined for\n`A ≥ 1`): `A=3 → +1`, `A=4 → −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.tauL4MeasuredOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.tauL4MeasuredOrder","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L116-L119","doc":"Measured A=4 leading Milnor order (#4378): `n ≈ 6.06`, consistent with\n`leadingOrder 4 = 6 = 2(4−1)`.  MEASURED, not proved — recorded for the record; no\ntheorem asserts `= 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.tauL4Measured_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.tauL4Measured_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L114-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.tauL4Measured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.tauL4Measured","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L107-L112","doc":"Measured genuine-Brunnian level trace at the substrate for A=4 (#4378, cited to\n`a4-h12-brunnian-deficit-measure.witness.json`, `w₄ = [[A₀₁,A₁₂],A₂₃]`):\n`τ_L₄ ≈ 1.000146 > 1`.  This is an empirically MEASURED input — NOT a proved\nclosed form.  Its arithmetic consequence (`< 1` fails, deficit `< 0`) is all that is\nused below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.tauBorromean_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.tauBorromean_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L94-L103","doc":"**A=3 sign, PROVED.**  `τ_Borr < 1` for `h ≠ 0` (physical regime `q ≠ 1`);\nhence the deficit `1 − τ_Borr > 0` and the cluster sign is `+`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.borromean_cofactor_pos_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.borromean_cofactor_pos_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L89-L92","doc":"The A=3 cofactor is strictly positive at `h = 0` (`= 3/4 ≠ 0`): the leading\nMilnor order is genuine, not an accidental extra vanishing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.borromean_deficit_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.borromean_deficit_order","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L80-L87","doc":"**A=3 order law, PROVED.**  The deficit factors as `h^(leadingOrder 3) · r(h)`\nwith cofactor `r(h) = (3 + h²)/(h² + 4)` — the leading power is exactly\n`h^(2(3−1)) = h⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.one_sub_tauBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.one_sub_tauBorromean","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L72-L78","doc":"**Trace-deficit closed form** (from #4360): `1 − τ_Borr = h⁴(3 + h²)/(h² + 4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.tauBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.tauBorromean","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L67-L70","doc":"The Borromean `H₃` Markov-trace closed form (restated from #4360's\n`QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanThreeBodyCluster.tauBorromean`):\n`τ_Borr(h) = (4 + h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶)/(h²+4)`, `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.leadingOrder_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.leadingOrder_four","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.leadingOrder_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.leadingOrder_three","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.leadingOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw.leadingOrder","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorParitySignLaw.lean#L59-L60","doc":"Leading Milnor order of the `A`-component Brunnian trace deficit, `2(A−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}